course: dictionary
lesson: 3224
title: Entertain: three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning fits. «There is no good evidence that ghosts are real; ghost stories are told mostly to entertain or scare.» Entertain sits beside scare, and stories are meant to hold our attention, so here entertain means to amuse people and keep them interested.
explain: The second meaning is about hosts. «Families entertain guests at home» means they invite visitors and give them food and drink. Swap in your meaning: if "invite and feed" fits the sentence, you have found the right one.
explain: The third meaning is about thinking. To entertain an idea is to think about it seriously. It does not mean to make it fun. Ask yourself what fits: you would not say "amuse an idea", so this meaning is different.
fact: Entertain means to amuse people and keep them interested, for example with a show, a joke or a game.
fact: «Gladiators fought in arenas to entertain crowds.» Here entertain means to keep the crowds watching and amused.
fact: To entertain guests means to invite them and give them food and drink.
fact: To entertain an idea means to think about it seriously.
fact: Entertain has four forms: entertain, entertains, entertained and entertaining.
exercise: «The clown made the children laugh and entertained the whole crowd.» What does entertained mean here? | Thought about them seriously | Made them go home early | *Kept them amused and interested | Gave them food and drink
exercise: Mum says, «We are going to entertain Auntie Rita on Sunday.» What does entertain mean? | *Invite her and give her food and drink | Think about her seriously | Make her cry | Hide from her
exercise: Copy the word from «Gladiators fought in arenas to entertain crowds» that means the people watching. | *crowds | arenas | gladiators | fought
test: The magician will entertain the children at the party. What does entertain mean? | Invite them and give them food | Hide from them | *Amuse them and keep them interested | Think about them carefully
test: Sam says he cannot entertain the idea of moving to a new school. What does he mean? | He will amuse the new school | He will invite the new school to tea | *He will not think about the idea seriously | He will sing about the new school
exam: Which sentence uses entertain to mean invite guests and give them food and drink? | *We will entertain our cousins at dinner tonight | The magician will entertain us with tricks | She could not entertain the thought for a second | The film entertained everyone in the cinema
